# Catatan deploy STB

When a change is ready for the STB server, add a release note in the same change. Ritual: `deploy/README.md`. Template: `deploy/releases/_template.md`.

## When to write one

Write `deploy/releases/pending/YYYY-MM-DD-nama-fitur.md` (today's date) when the work changes what STB runs: API behavior, migration, env, or seed data.

Skip it for docs-only edits, FE prompts under `docs/requests/`, and refactors with no runtime or schema change.

## What to put in it

Copy the template. Keep all four sections. Write **Tidak ada.** when a section does not apply.

- **Env** — list new keys and why. Add the same keys to `.env.example` and `.env.docker.example`. Do not put secret values in the note.
- **Migration** — filename under `src/database/migrations/`. STB applies it on container start (`SKIP_MIGRATE` stays `false`).
- **Data awal** — `scripts/deploy.sh` does not run seeders. Seeders stay manual (`npm run seed`) and wipe demo data, so never set `RUN_SEED=true` on STB. A new fixed value (module, status, kind) is a TypeScript constant plus a migration that adds it to the MySQL ENUM only when the column does not already have it (`enumHasValue` in `src/database/migrations/20260815100000_create_family_core.ts`). After that migration has run, the value lives in the DB. Do not add a seeder for it.
- **Cek setelah naik** — `curl -fsS http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health`, plus one check specific to the change when there is one.

Do not put deploy notes in `docs/requests/`.

## Do not mark shipped

Leave the file in `pending/`. Move it to `deploy/releases/shipped/` only after the user says the STB deploy succeeded.
